****npm install redux-persist***
once user logins if he refresh all the data will be gone to not to happen that we use -npm install redux-persist

****npm install cookie-parser**** in route directory once it is installed initalize in index.js

The cookie is like an envelope, and the token is the letter inside. cookie-parser opens the envelope so your server can read the letter.

why it is used to verify user hy we use cookie-parser

Because the token that proves who the user is lives in a cookie, and cookie-parser is what lets your server read it.

The chain of reasoning

1.After login, the server gives the browser a token (JWT) inside a cookie.
2.The browser automatically sends that cookie with every request. This is how the server “remembers” the user, since HTTP itself has no memory between requests.
3.The cookie arrives as one raw string in the Cookie header, like token=eyJhbGci...; theme=dark.
To verify the user, your server needs just the token value so it can run jwt.verify() on it.
4.cookie-parser converts that raw string into req.cookies.token, so you can grab it easily.


